# Terraform

Write readable, least-privilege, reviewable infrastructure code. Prefer a clear
file split from the start — not one monolith `.tf`. Validation and
`templatefile()` conventions: `terraform-validation`.

## File layout

| File | Holds |
|------|--------|
| `provider.tf` | `terraform` block, required providers, provider configs |
| `variables.tf` | input `variable` blocks |
| `locals.tf` | `locals` |
| `main.tf` | primary resources (or the composition entrypoint) |
| `outputs.tf` | `output` blocks |

- Segregate by concern; when `main.tf` mixes unrelated resources, split into
  named files (`network.tf`, `iam.tf`, …)
- Don’t create empty stub files; do create the standard files once that
  concern exists
- Prefer small reusable modules over copy-pasting whole stacks

## Docs & comments

- Every `.tf` file starts with a short header comment (what it owns)
- Every `variable` and `output` has a useful `description`
- Comment non-obvious locals/resources — never narrate obvious HCL
- Follow `code-comments`

## Values via locals (single source of truth)

- Resources, data sources, and modules read `local.*` only — not scattered
  `var.*` or inline expressions
- `variables.tf` = external input contract; `locals.tf` = internal value
  catalog
- Swapping variable → data source / remote state / formula should usually
  touch `locals.tf` (+ maybe `variables.tf`), not the resource graph

```hcl
variable "environment" {
  type        = string
  description = "Deployment environment name"
}

locals {
  environment = var.environment
  name_prefix = "app-${local.environment}"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "this" {
  cidr_block = local.vpc_cidr
  tags       = { Name = "${local.name_prefix}-vpc" }
}
```

## Resources & style

- Prefer `for_each` over `count` when resources are keyed by identity
- Pin provider and module versions; avoid unconstrained `>=` in shared
  modules
- Resource labels: short purpose-based snake_case
- Consistent `tags` / `default_tags`; run as if `terraform fmt` + `validate`
  are required
- Prefer hardcoded literal image tags on resources (tag only — no digest)
  when Renovate or similar tooling must see them

## Safety

- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, or private keys in `.tf` / checked-in
  `.tfvars`
- Prefer data sources and remote state over duplicating IDs across stacks
- Call out destructive changes (replace, destroy, force-new) before applying
- Scope IAM / security groups narrowly; avoid `*` unless required and
  documented

## Anti-patterns

```hcl
# ❌ BAD — resources read vars directly; opaque count index
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "b" {
  count  = length(var.names)
  bucket = var.names[count.index]
}

# ✅ GOOD — inputs → locals → resources; for_each by identity
locals { buckets = var.buckets }
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "this" {
  for_each = local.buckets
  bucket   = each.value
}
```
